1
00:01:51,077 --> 00:01:55,077
If cotton hair is true, could everything they said be true as well?

2
00:01:55,077 --> 00:01:59,077
If I can just get back to Kokoyashi Village, I'm sure I could figure it all out.

3
00:01:59,077 --> 00:02:02,077
But without a decent ship, how am I gonna get there?

4
00:02:02,077 --> 00:02:05,077
And I'm on the Grand Line of all places.

5
00:02:05,077 --> 00:02:10,077
According to this math, it's impossible to sail directly from this sea to the East Blue.

6
00:02:15,077 --> 00:02:18,077
Wait! What's that?!

7
00:02:18,077 --> 00:02:20,077
You're the captain?!

8
00:02:21,077 --> 00:02:24,077
Aw, man! That was a lucky break. If I hadn't gotten my memory back,

9
00:02:24,077 --> 00:02:27,077
I would've been stuck eye-eyeing Captain Usopp forever.

10
00:02:27,077 --> 00:02:29,077
Shut your mouth! I'm never gonna believe it!

11
00:02:29,077 --> 00:02:33,077
No matter what anyone says, I know that I'm the Great Captain Usopp!

12
00:02:33,077 --> 00:02:36,077
I have an army of 8,000 pirates who obey my every command!

13
00:02:38,077 --> 00:02:40,077
That's the Usopp I know through and through!

14
00:02:40,077 --> 00:02:44,077
But you're not the captain. You're Usopp, the sniper of the Straw Hat Pirates!

15
00:02:44,077 --> 00:02:47,077
Crap! The tables have turned against me.

16
00:02:47,077 --> 00:02:51,077
This guy's a monster just like me, and yet he's the captain?

17
00:02:51,077 --> 00:02:53,077
Hey, Chopper!

18
00:02:53,077 --> 00:02:55,077
Keep away!

19
00:02:56,077 --> 00:02:58,077
Aw, come on! How long are you gonna act like that?

20
00:02:59,077 --> 00:03:01,077
Let's play like we always do!

21
00:03:01,077 --> 00:03:05,077
So, I'm the ship's doctor, and this is something I always do?

22
00:03:05,077 --> 00:03:09,077
Yeah! You do it every time we have a party! It's like your thing!

23
00:03:10,077 --> 00:03:11,077
Come on, Chopper!

24
00:03:11,077 --> 00:03:12,077
Come on, Chopper!

25
00:03:12,077 --> 00:03:17,077
That rubber monkey said he got his memories back, yet he's acting just as much of an idiot as before.

26
00:03:17,077 --> 00:03:18,077
Huh.

27
00:03:18,077 --> 00:03:21,077
That's right. The captain never ever changes, no matter what happens to him.

28
00:03:22,077 --> 00:03:26,077
Even if I am a pirate, I'm nothing compared to these freaks of nature.

29
00:03:26,077 --> 00:03:30,077
I'd never survive sailing with the likes of them. How did I get myself into this mess?

30
00:03:30,077 --> 00:03:35,077
Now it's clear what happened. Everyone didn't miraculously lose their memories overnight.

31
00:03:35,077 --> 00:03:38,077
They were stolen, and so the obvious culprit is...

32
00:03:38,077 --> 00:03:41,077
The only person we all remember, that brat.

33
00:03:41,077 --> 00:03:44,077
What would that freaky kid want with our memories anyway?

34
00:03:44,077 --> 00:03:45,077
Beats me.

35
00:03:46,077 --> 00:03:47,077
Wait a sec!

36
00:03:48,077 --> 00:03:53,077
We have to get Nami and Zoro back! Come on! Let's go!

37
00:03:54,077 --> 00:03:56,077
You're right, but we should wait until morning.

38
00:03:57,077 --> 00:03:58,077
Why can't we go right now?

39
00:03:58,077 --> 00:04:03,077
Searching for two people on an unknown island in the middle of the night is a recipe for disaster.

40
00:04:03,077 --> 00:04:05,077
Oh. Guess you got a point.

41
00:04:06,077 --> 00:04:09,077
Let's get some rest, and then we'll begin our search when the sun comes up.

42
00:04:09,077 --> 00:04:13,077
I don't think that boy will be back tonight. We gave him a lot of trouble.

43
00:04:13,077 --> 00:04:15,077
He'll think twice before showing up here again.

44
00:04:16,077 --> 00:04:21,077
Hmm. Right! It's settled! We'll rest up and start the search first thing in the morning!

45
00:04:21,077 --> 00:04:26,077
Hold on a sec. I'm all for bringing that lovely lady Nami back, but not that Zoro guy.

46
00:04:26,077 --> 00:04:28,077
He can just stay gone for all I care.

47
00:04:28,077 --> 00:04:33,077
I agree! If you two want to go look for him, you can do it on your own!

48
00:04:33,077 --> 00:04:35,077
I, uh, I'm not sure.

49
00:04:35,077 --> 00:04:37,077
What the? What are you saying?

50
00:04:37,077 --> 00:04:39,077
We're saying why look for Zoro.

51
00:04:39,077 --> 00:04:44,077
He's a pirate hunter, remember? Why should we go through all the trouble of chasing down a guy like that?

52
00:04:45,077 --> 00:04:48,077
Isn't it obvious? Because he's our friend.

53
00:04:49,077 --> 00:04:52,077
Just because you said it doesn't mean it's true. Come on.

54
00:04:52,077 --> 00:04:56,077
That guy sure didn't act like he was our friend. Surely you noticed that.

55
00:04:57,077 --> 00:05:00,077
The way he left is proof enough for me.

56
00:05:03,077 --> 00:05:11,077
Usopp is the sniper, Sanji is the cook, Chopper is the doctor, Robin is the archaeologist, Nami is the navigator, and Zoro is the swordsman.

57
00:05:12,077 --> 00:05:15,077
We are the Straw Hat Pirates, and we don't leave any man behind!

58
00:05:16,077 --> 00:05:19,077
Then we'll have to get Mr. Swordsman's memory back.

59
00:05:19,077 --> 00:05:25,077
No problem! All I have to do is kick that brat's butt again! That's how I got mine back! Sound good, Chopper?

60
00:05:26,077 --> 00:05:29,077
Well, it looks like tomorrow's gonna be a really busy day.

61
00:05:29,077 --> 00:05:31,077
Alright, let's all get some sleep while we can!

62
00:05:34,077 --> 00:05:38,077
The key to unraveling this mystery is somewhere on that island.

63
00:05:38,077 --> 00:05:50,077
It seems that I underestimated you, Monkey D. Luffy. You're a formidable enemy.

64
00:05:51,077 --> 00:05:54,077
Still, you won't stop me from making my wish come true.

65
00:05:55,077 --> 00:05:58,077
But in order to do so, I'll need an ally.

66
00:05:58,077 --> 00:05:59,077
An ally.

67
00:06:02,077 --> 00:06:04,077
An ally like a certain skilled swordsman.

68
00:06:05,077 --> 00:06:08,077
That's right. He's different than he was yesterday.

69
00:06:08,077 --> 00:06:13,077
This man is Pirate Hunter Zoro. If I try to approach him, things could go bad quickly.

70
00:06:14,077 --> 00:06:18,077
Okay, then. I'll cut my losses for tonight. There'll be other chances soon, anyway.

71
00:06:18,077 --> 00:06:21,077
Oh, yes. And when that time comes, your work will truly begin.

72
00:06:21,077 --> 00:06:28,077
It is said that fish from around the world gathered together in the All Blue.

73
00:06:28,657 --> 00:06:30,197
I'll cut my losses for tonight.

74
00:06:30,597 --> 00:06:32,637
There'll be other chances soon, anyway.

75
00:06:34,097 --> 00:06:35,137
Oh, yes.

76
00:06:35,437 --> 00:06:38,357
And when that time comes, your work will truly begin.

77
00:06:46,077 --> 00:06:48,897
It is said that fish from around the world

78
00:06:48,897 --> 00:06:50,677
gathered together in the all-blue

79
00:06:50,677 --> 00:06:53,257
have dreamed of reaching that sea.

80
00:06:56,497 --> 00:06:58,017
Why'd you help me?

81
00:06:58,557 --> 00:07:01,697
It doesn't make sense to sacrifice so much for me,

82
00:07:01,917 --> 00:07:02,957
you old fool!

83
00:07:03,517 --> 00:07:04,177
Tell me!

84
00:07:04,357 --> 00:07:06,257
Because for my entire life,

85
00:07:06,337 --> 00:07:08,017
I've had the same dream as you.

86
00:07:09,217 --> 00:07:10,237
A restaurant?

87
00:07:10,657 --> 00:07:13,417
I was thinking that if I make it out of this mess alive,

88
00:07:13,557 --> 00:07:16,197
I'd like to build a restaurant as my final purpose.

89
00:07:16,557 --> 00:07:16,917
Great!

90
00:07:17,217 --> 00:07:18,617
And I'll even help you do it!

91
00:07:18,837 --> 00:07:19,957
So don't die, okay?

92
00:07:20,777 --> 00:07:22,897
A weak little brat like you

93
00:07:22,897 --> 00:07:24,317
couldn't be much good for anything.

94
00:07:25,277 --> 00:07:26,917
Then I'll become strong!

95
00:07:26,917 --> 00:07:31,597
That annoying old geezer saved my life.

96
00:07:31,797 --> 00:07:33,837
There's no way I would have ever left him.

97
00:07:34,137 --> 00:07:34,837
So why?

98
00:07:35,377 --> 00:07:36,857
What the hell happened to me?

99
00:07:36,857 --> 00:07:44,537
Pepper, carrot, onion.

100
00:07:44,537 --> 00:07:47,157
I wonder what happened to the Usopp pirates.

101
00:07:47,157 --> 00:07:52,677
It's go time, brave Usopp pirates!

102
00:07:52,677 --> 00:07:55,277
We do have a village that we need to protect!

103
00:07:55,617 --> 00:07:58,317
So what adventure are you going to tell me about today?

104
00:07:58,817 --> 00:07:59,737
Well, let's see.

105
00:08:00,177 --> 00:08:00,797
Oh, I know.

106
00:08:01,017 --> 00:08:05,677
What about the story of me fighting a giant goldfish at the South Pole when I was only five years old?

107
00:08:06,677 --> 00:08:07,177
Goldfish?

108
00:08:07,177 --> 00:08:08,697
A giant goldfish!

109
00:08:08,857 --> 00:08:11,637
What first astounded me was the immense size of its poop!

110
00:08:11,857 --> 00:08:15,097
It was so big that when I landed on it, I thought it was solid ground!

111
00:08:15,097 --> 00:08:15,637
Usopp!

112
00:08:15,637 --> 00:08:21,277
I always dreamed of being a pirate just like my old man.

113
00:08:21,817 --> 00:08:25,637
But did I actually become a real one, leaving everyone behind to do so?

114
00:08:25,637 --> 00:08:30,697
Why am I here?

115
00:08:31,157 --> 00:08:32,937
Why am I here with these humans?

116
00:08:33,617 --> 00:08:36,877
The only ones I've ever trusted were Dr. Herilook and Dr. Eam.

117
00:08:37,357 --> 00:08:40,337
Even among my fellow reindeer, I had no friends.

118
00:08:40,837 --> 00:08:42,037
I was always alone.

119
00:08:43,357 --> 00:08:45,997
I promise I'm not going to shoot you, see?

120
00:08:47,937 --> 00:08:50,037
Listen, my name is Herilook!

121
00:08:50,417 --> 00:08:51,597
Dr. Herilook!

122
00:08:51,597 --> 00:08:55,757
And if that's true, there's no disease that can't be cured.

123
00:08:56,017 --> 00:08:57,417
Let them all laugh at me.

124
00:08:57,477 --> 00:08:58,177
I don't care.

125
00:08:58,417 --> 00:09:01,317
My medical skills will save this country yet, you'll see.

126
00:09:01,757 --> 00:09:05,917
I raised this skull and crossbones to challenge all diseases of the world.

127
00:09:06,397 --> 00:09:07,137
A skull?

128
00:09:07,517 --> 00:09:11,977
This symbol represents my conviction and belief that there is nothing that's impossible.

129
00:09:12,537 --> 00:09:15,697
I will save this country with my doctor's skills.

130
00:09:16,817 --> 00:09:18,477
And now I have friends?

131
00:09:19,077 --> 00:09:19,937
Six of them?

132
00:09:19,937 --> 00:09:25,097
How am I supposed to believe I'm out here with them as a doctor on a pirate ship?

133
00:09:26,377 --> 00:09:28,857
But what if it's true?

134
00:09:32,097 --> 00:09:33,577
None of that's going to happen.

135
00:09:34,117 --> 00:09:35,777
Nothing can take away my dreams.

136
00:09:36,217 --> 00:09:38,337
And I know it's the same for you guys, too.

137
00:09:40,937 --> 00:09:41,717
Here, here, here.

138
00:09:41,717 --> 00:09:41,877
Here.

139
00:09:41,877 --> 00:10:08,557
Here, here.

140
00:10:08,557 --> 00:10:14,017
Nami, Zoro, sit tight and don't worry, we're coming for you.

141
00:10:16,277 --> 00:10:17,637
Hey, wake up!

142
00:10:17,717 --> 00:10:18,997
We're already up and ready.

143
00:10:19,497 --> 00:10:21,517
Mr. Cook and Mr. Doctor are here too.

144
00:10:23,657 --> 00:10:26,437
There's no way I'd ever leave a lady like that behind.

145
00:10:26,757 --> 00:10:29,257
And besides, Robin's gonna need herself a bodyguard.

146
00:10:29,277 --> 00:10:33,017
And if anyone gets injured, then they'll surely need the assistance of a doctor, right?

147
00:10:33,337 --> 00:10:35,917
Which means that I should stay behind and guard the ship.

148
00:10:35,997 --> 00:10:37,277
You're coming too, Usopp.

149
00:10:37,277 --> 00:10:39,017
Well, actually, I've got this.

150
00:10:39,377 --> 00:10:41,757
My heart'll stop if I go on the island disease.

151
00:10:42,457 --> 00:10:43,797
Just come with us.

152
00:10:43,877 --> 00:10:44,837
I know one thing.

153
00:10:45,477 --> 00:10:49,877
Usopp, the brave warrior of the sea, is a man who always comes through when things get rough.

154
00:10:50,237 --> 00:10:50,957
That's me.

155
00:10:51,537 --> 00:10:53,617
All right then, we're all going!

156
00:10:54,337 --> 00:10:55,117
Oh, crap.

157
00:10:55,377 --> 00:10:56,917
I got caught up in the moment.

158
00:10:57,237 --> 00:10:59,677
So, how are we gonna get across the bay to the island?

159
00:11:00,077 --> 00:11:02,177
I think a raft is the most viable option.

160
00:11:02,477 --> 00:11:03,137
Good idea.

161
00:11:03,337 --> 00:11:05,117
Hey, make us a raft, Usopp.

162
00:11:05,117 --> 00:11:06,177
Why should I?

163
00:11:06,177 --> 00:11:08,937
I'm Captain Usopp, remember?

164
00:11:09,357 --> 00:11:10,177
Yeah, yeah.

165
00:11:10,657 --> 00:11:12,457
At the very least, I'm a sniper.

166
00:11:12,917 --> 00:11:15,677
Either way, I can't properly do the job of a shipwright.

167
00:11:16,477 --> 00:11:19,617
To make a raft, all you do is tie some locks together.

168
00:11:20,597 --> 00:11:21,737
Problem solved.

169
00:11:22,197 --> 00:11:24,617
Are you sure those are the right kinds of knots to use?

170
00:11:25,277 --> 00:11:25,817
Well, yeah.

171
00:11:25,957 --> 00:11:26,817
A knot's a knot, right?

172
00:11:26,957 --> 00:11:28,157
You've gotta be kidding.

173
00:11:28,597 --> 00:11:31,097
That thing's gonna break apart as soon as it hits the water.

174
00:11:31,097 --> 00:11:33,617
But mine looks a whole lot cooler.

175
00:11:34,237 --> 00:11:35,677
Check this baby out.

176
00:11:36,677 --> 00:11:37,517
No way.

177
00:11:37,777 --> 00:11:38,717
Mine is the coolest.

178
00:11:39,337 --> 00:11:40,797
Sorry, but there's no comparison.

179
00:11:41,617 --> 00:11:42,497
Mine rules.

180
00:11:42,617 --> 00:11:43,577
Oh, come on.

181
00:11:43,697 --> 00:11:44,197
Seriously?

182
00:11:44,197 --> 00:11:47,977
How can you call yourselves pirates when you can't even make a decent raft?

183
00:11:50,237 --> 00:11:52,317
Such amazing workmanship.

184
00:11:52,657 --> 00:11:53,037
See?

185
00:11:53,177 --> 00:11:55,197
Usopp's a man who always comes through.

186
00:11:56,197 --> 00:11:56,757
Wait.

187
00:11:57,097 --> 00:11:58,897
How do I know how to build this thing?

188
00:11:59,137 --> 00:12:00,117
I don't get it.

189
00:12:00,377 --> 00:12:00,897
All right.

190
00:12:01,357 --> 00:12:02,497
Let's go!

191
00:12:02,497 --> 00:12:10,757
Thanks for the room.

192
00:12:10,997 --> 00:12:11,857
What do I owe you?

193
00:12:12,037 --> 00:12:13,377
Uh, sorry.

194
00:12:13,517 --> 00:12:14,037
Who are you?

195
00:12:14,257 --> 00:12:14,477
Huh?

196
00:12:15,017 --> 00:12:15,457
What?

197
00:12:15,597 --> 00:12:16,597
I'm a guest of the inn.

198
00:12:16,677 --> 00:12:17,897
I stayed here last night.

199
00:12:18,117 --> 00:12:19,237
Do you recognize her?

200
00:12:19,357 --> 00:12:20,897
No, I've never seen her before.

201
00:12:21,117 --> 00:12:21,757
Uh...

202
00:12:21,757 --> 00:12:22,237
Wait.

203
00:12:22,497 --> 00:12:23,757
She might be a thief.

204
00:12:24,317 --> 00:12:24,577
What?

205
00:12:24,757 --> 00:12:25,317
A thief?

206
00:12:25,477 --> 00:12:26,997
Hey, now hold on a second.

207
00:12:27,097 --> 00:12:27,937
I'm a customer.

208
00:12:28,597 --> 00:12:30,637
I just met all three of you yesterday.

209
00:12:30,637 --> 00:12:33,177
Do you seriously not remember me?

210
00:12:33,317 --> 00:12:35,237
I mean, surely you do, Mr. Manager.

211
00:12:35,937 --> 00:12:36,417
Manager?

212
00:12:36,997 --> 00:12:37,857
You mean me?

213
00:12:38,117 --> 00:12:40,897
Uh, he is the manager of this inn, right?

214
00:12:40,997 --> 00:12:42,037
I don't know.

215
00:12:42,317 --> 00:12:42,637
Huh?

216
00:12:47,677 --> 00:12:51,937
It's nice that I got to stay for free and all, but what in the world is going on here?

217
00:12:53,177 --> 00:12:54,637
Could this mean that...

218
00:12:55,637 --> 00:12:57,437
Who are you?

219
00:12:57,757 --> 00:12:59,957
Don't tell me you've lost your memories, too.

220
00:13:00,637 --> 00:13:04,717
It's just like what happened to me yesterday.

221
00:13:07,017 --> 00:13:07,457
Yesterday?

222
00:13:08,157 --> 00:13:09,117
Yeah, that's right.

223
00:13:09,357 --> 00:13:10,757
They might have come through here.

224
00:13:11,217 --> 00:13:14,277
There was a swordsman with green hair and a woman driving a weird boat.

225
00:13:14,517 --> 00:13:15,357
So did you see him?

226
00:13:15,797 --> 00:13:16,197
Yesterday.

227
00:13:16,597 --> 00:13:17,937
Now, what did I do yesterday?

228
00:13:18,237 --> 00:13:19,477
Ah, not you two!

229
00:13:19,697 --> 00:13:21,757
What is wrong with the people on this crazy island?

230
00:13:21,937 --> 00:13:25,117
Not a single one of these nitwits remembers anything about what they did yesterday!

231
00:13:25,117 --> 00:13:27,937
What carefree people?

232
00:13:28,377 --> 00:13:30,557
I think it's a little more than being carefree.

233
00:13:30,737 --> 00:13:32,477
And we're not really ones to talk.

234
00:13:32,537 --> 00:13:32,697
Huh?

235
00:13:32,837 --> 00:13:33,857
We're just like them.

236
00:13:34,337 --> 00:13:36,557
It might be more than just coincidence.

237
00:13:37,057 --> 00:13:38,177
So what's the plan?

238
00:13:38,277 --> 00:13:38,937
What do we do?

239
00:13:39,657 --> 00:13:42,057
It'll be kind of tough finding them in this situation.

240
00:13:42,537 --> 00:13:42,857
Right!

241
00:13:43,077 --> 00:13:44,137
Back to the ship, then!

242
00:13:44,137 --> 00:13:47,617
No good thing is going to come from us wandering around on this creepy island.

243
00:13:47,937 --> 00:13:49,057
So, what do you say?

244
00:13:50,937 --> 00:13:51,897
Hey, Nami!

245
00:13:52,457 --> 00:13:53,377
Oh, crap!

246
00:13:54,817 --> 00:13:55,377
Hey!

247
00:13:56,737 --> 00:13:57,257
Wait!

248
00:13:59,497 --> 00:14:00,057
Ah!

249
00:14:03,477 --> 00:14:06,637
What a day.

250
00:14:06,637 --> 00:14:09,337
Why'd you run away from us, Nami?

251
00:14:09,557 --> 00:14:11,817
You'll never get this away from me, got it?

252
00:14:11,937 --> 00:14:13,897
You'd have to kill me before I'd let it go.

253
00:14:14,117 --> 00:14:14,977
Don't say that.

254
00:14:15,037 --> 00:14:17,417
There's no way I'd hurt a beautiful lady like you.

255
00:14:17,617 --> 00:14:18,497
That's ridiculous.

256
00:14:19,257 --> 00:14:21,417
I promise I won't lay a finger on you.

257
00:14:21,737 --> 00:14:23,177
Though I'd really like to.

258
00:14:23,977 --> 00:14:26,257
Hey, Doc, what kind of disease does he have?

259
00:14:26,357 --> 00:14:27,657
Can't you do anything for him?

260
00:14:27,717 --> 00:14:30,977
It's definitely a serious condition, but I'm pretty sure there's no cure.

261
00:14:31,257 --> 00:14:31,617
Fine.

262
00:14:31,757 --> 00:14:32,537
Let's make a deal.

263
00:14:33,057 --> 00:14:33,977
What kind of deal?

264
00:14:33,977 --> 00:14:39,737
I promise to give you 10% of my treasure if you promise to take me back to Kokoyashi Village.

265
00:14:39,917 --> 00:14:40,597
No way.

266
00:14:40,957 --> 00:14:42,497
Okay, then 20%.

267
00:14:42,497 --> 00:14:43,277
Nuh-uh.

268
00:14:43,537 --> 00:14:44,837
Fine, 30%.

269
00:14:44,837 --> 00:14:45,677
Can't do it.

270
00:14:45,877 --> 00:14:47,637
It'll kill me, but 50%.

271
00:14:47,637 --> 00:14:48,257
Sorry.

272
00:14:50,757 --> 00:14:53,797
Just how much of this treasure are you trying to swindle me out of?

273
00:14:53,957 --> 00:14:55,937
Come on, Nami, you love that treasure.

274
00:14:56,897 --> 00:14:59,257
There's no way you'd ever give it up to anybody.

275
00:14:59,677 --> 00:15:02,497
Hey, how the heck did you know that I was going to double cross you?

276
00:15:03,977 --> 00:15:06,497
Because we're friends, Nami.

277
00:15:06,617 --> 00:15:07,297
How else?

278
00:15:07,877 --> 00:15:08,857
Give me a break.

279
00:15:08,937 --> 00:15:10,997
Why would I ever be friends with the likes of you?

280
00:15:11,537 --> 00:15:12,637
This is ridiculous.

281
00:15:12,817 --> 00:15:14,077
The negotiations are over.

282
00:15:14,177 --> 00:15:14,637
I'm leaving.

283
00:15:14,877 --> 00:15:15,257
See ya.

284
00:15:17,737 --> 00:15:19,097
Step aside, please.

285
00:15:19,217 --> 00:15:19,877
Not happening.

286
00:15:20,477 --> 00:15:23,017
Nami, you are going to come along with us.

287
00:15:23,257 --> 00:15:24,797
You're out of your freaking mind.

288
00:15:24,797 --> 00:15:26,937
Why would I go anywhere with you guys?

289
00:15:27,117 --> 00:15:28,117
Now move it, jerk!

290
00:15:28,497 --> 00:15:29,437
I won't.

291
00:15:31,157 --> 00:15:32,137
Miss Navigator.

292
00:15:32,517 --> 00:15:32,777
Huh?

293
00:15:33,377 --> 00:15:37,797
You've been feeling that there's something odd about this island ever since you set foot on it.

294
00:15:38,617 --> 00:15:39,657
Am I wrong?

295
00:15:39,657 --> 00:15:46,217
You look perplexed.

296
00:15:46,317 --> 00:15:47,097
What's the matter?

297
00:15:47,837 --> 00:15:49,897
There was a boy holding a strange horn.

298
00:15:50,317 --> 00:15:52,777
Yeah, last night I got a good punch in on him.

299
00:15:53,057 --> 00:15:57,677
And then some smoke came out of his horn and then it went into my body and then I could remember stuff.

300
00:15:57,797 --> 00:15:58,457
That's right.

301
00:15:58,657 --> 00:16:00,697
The captain has all of his memories back.

302
00:16:01,597 --> 00:16:02,037
Preposterous.

303
00:16:02,237 --> 00:16:03,617
Are you sure you weren't dreaming?

304
00:16:04,017 --> 00:16:04,837
No, it's true.

305
00:16:05,317 --> 00:16:07,977
I saw the whole thing happen with my own two eyes.

306
00:16:08,317 --> 00:16:12,097
I also seem to remember seeing that little brat the night before last as well.

307
00:16:12,317 --> 00:16:14,297
What I want to know is why he came back.

308
00:16:14,417 --> 00:16:18,517
It's just a theory, but maybe he wasn't able to steal all of your memories in one shot.

309
00:16:18,777 --> 00:16:24,217
Even with just what I know, you all seem to have experienced numerous incredible adventures during your journeys together.

310
00:16:24,217 --> 00:16:28,297
It was too much to take all at once, so he starved himself and returned yesterday?

311
00:16:28,737 --> 00:16:30,617
The theory seems logical enough.

312
00:16:30,657 --> 00:16:33,057
Hey, Robin, do you think that memories taste good?

313
00:16:33,057 --> 00:16:36,317
So then, that little boy...

314
00:16:36,317 --> 00:16:36,797
Bye!

315
00:16:36,977 --> 00:16:37,457
See ya!

316
00:16:39,297 --> 00:16:40,277
All right then!

317
00:16:40,617 --> 00:16:44,497
Let's go kick that little runt's butt again and get everybody's memories back!

318
00:16:44,737 --> 00:16:46,697
Then Zoro will rejoin our crew!

319
00:16:47,117 --> 00:16:52,337
I doubt that it's going to be as simple as that, but we definitely need to give that brat some painful payback.

320
00:16:52,937 --> 00:16:54,857
Look, can't we just forget about Zoro?

321
00:16:54,857 --> 00:17:01,757
Zoro, even if we get our memories back, it's kind of unsettling to be in a pirate crew on a pirate ship with a pirate hunter, you know?

322
00:17:01,997 --> 00:17:04,257
Zoro's the swordsman and Nami's the navigator.

323
00:17:04,417 --> 00:17:06,277
They're our friends and part of our crew!

324
00:17:06,377 --> 00:17:08,577
It still bothers me when you say that, you know!

325
00:17:08,797 --> 00:17:11,597
How can I be a pirate, much less friends with pirates?

326
00:17:11,957 --> 00:17:14,357
Look, I'm the one who's going to be bothered without you.

327
00:17:14,657 --> 00:17:17,597
Without a navigator, the ship can't go anywhere, understand?

328
00:17:17,597 --> 00:17:21,877
Robin, do you have any idea where that little runt is hiding?

329
00:17:22,237 --> 00:17:25,197
Well, there is one place that I'd like to check out.

330
00:17:25,777 --> 00:17:27,317
Okay then, let's go!

331
00:17:27,377 --> 00:17:28,477
Hey, wait, Michael!

332
00:17:28,857 --> 00:17:31,157
Don't worry, I'll carry the lady's stuff!

333
00:17:31,457 --> 00:17:35,377
If doing so means I get to be with you, then this is no trouble at all!

334
00:17:35,817 --> 00:17:37,897
Eh, got a bad feeling about this.

335
00:17:40,317 --> 00:17:43,257
Even with everything that's happening, they all follow Luffy.

336
00:17:43,777 --> 00:17:46,177
I wonder if it's true that I have friends now.

337
00:17:47,597 --> 00:17:49,897
Hey, Chopper, what are you waiting for?

338
00:17:49,977 --> 00:17:50,837
Let's go!

339
00:17:51,877 --> 00:17:52,617
Aye, aye!

340
00:18:17,597 --> 00:18:24,417
If you want to eat, help yourself.

341
00:18:24,557 --> 00:18:29,317
Well, it's true that I am rather hungry, but this isn't the kind of food that I eat.

342
00:18:29,657 --> 00:18:30,297
Oh, yeah?

343
00:18:31,137 --> 00:18:33,617
Tell me, why haven't you asked me who I am yet?

344
00:18:34,397 --> 00:18:35,657
Ah, that's right.

345
00:18:35,757 --> 00:18:38,217
The people that live on this island don't remember anything.

346
00:18:38,557 --> 00:18:40,177
Not even their own names, huh?

347
00:18:40,177 --> 00:18:41,677
No point in asking.

348
00:18:43,457 --> 00:18:46,357
You're on a quest to become the strongest in the world, right?

349
00:18:47,217 --> 00:18:47,617
Hmm.

350
00:18:48,397 --> 00:18:53,477
If that's the case, then I think that Monkey D. Luffy would be the perfect opponent for you.

351
00:18:54,637 --> 00:18:55,797
Hi, I'm Luffy!

352
00:18:55,957 --> 00:18:56,697
So what's your name?

353
00:18:57,557 --> 00:18:59,477
Talking about that idiot in the straw hat?

354
00:18:59,477 --> 00:19:05,117
I'm actually surprised that someone like Roro Noah Zoro couldn't see that man's strength.

355
00:19:05,337 --> 00:19:06,257
See his strength?

356
00:19:06,357 --> 00:19:06,917
What do you mean?

357
00:19:07,137 --> 00:19:12,697
I mean that Monkey D. Luffy destroyed the vicious Arlong along with his fishmen pirate crew in the East Blue.

358
00:19:13,037 --> 00:19:18,897
Then in the Grand Line, he managed to bring down Crocodile, one of the seven warlords of the sea, all by himself.

359
00:19:19,377 --> 00:19:20,437
Warlords of the sea?

360
00:19:20,437 --> 00:19:22,097
Yeah, and that's not all.

361
00:19:22,637 --> 00:19:25,917
On the Sky Islands, he beat up a powerful god named Eneru.

362
00:19:26,497 --> 00:19:29,637
And after that, he went on a rampage in a marine base.

363
00:19:29,757 --> 00:19:32,357
Against Luffy, even the marines had to throw in the towel.

364
00:19:33,157 --> 00:19:35,217
I've never seen another pirate like him.

365
00:19:36,357 --> 00:19:37,637
Don't screw with me.

366
00:19:37,957 --> 00:19:41,237
I'm not in the mood for any more of these cock and bull stories, you got it?

367
00:19:43,597 --> 00:19:47,197
So, after hearing all that, you want to fight Luffy, don't you?

368
00:19:50,437 --> 00:19:54,417
What are you doing?

369
00:19:54,417 --> 00:19:56,417
What are you doing?

370
00:20:10,417 --> 00:20:12,557
Where are we?

371
00:20:12,557 --> 00:20:21,537
Is this where that weird kid lives?

372
00:20:21,797 --> 00:20:23,957
This place is giving me the creeps!

373
00:20:24,677 --> 00:20:26,397
Did I catch a cold or something?

374
00:20:26,717 --> 00:20:28,577
I've been shivering for a while now.

375
00:20:29,217 --> 00:20:30,837
If only we had a doctor here.

376
00:20:32,177 --> 00:20:33,537
Wait, that's me!

377
00:20:33,537 --> 00:20:41,377
I bet these pirates are trying to take me out to the middle of nowhere so they can steal my gold!

378
00:20:42,557 --> 00:20:45,097
I won't let them do it!

379
00:20:46,837 --> 00:20:49,397
Nami's been shooting glances at me this whole time!

380
00:20:49,677 --> 00:20:51,037
That can only mean one thing!

381
00:20:51,377 --> 00:20:52,997
She's fallen in love with me!

382
00:20:54,977 --> 00:20:55,917
Back at ya!

383
00:20:56,417 --> 00:20:59,177
Is that some kind of signal that he's about to steal my gold?

384
00:20:59,257 --> 00:21:00,257
He's freaking me out!

385
00:21:01,197 --> 00:21:02,217
Now I see.

386
00:21:02,537 --> 00:21:03,057
Butterfly!

387
00:21:04,737 --> 00:21:05,737
What's up, Robin?

388
00:21:05,797 --> 00:21:06,737
Did you find something?

389
00:21:06,737 --> 00:21:10,337
I just determined the culprit that stole your memories.

390
00:21:10,937 --> 00:21:13,557
Consequently, it's not the one we thought it was.

391
00:21:13,737 --> 00:21:14,777
Wait a second.

392
00:21:14,857 --> 00:21:16,237
You mean it's not that little brat?

393
00:21:16,617 --> 00:21:19,417
Now, let's make our way to the Sea God's Palace.

394
00:21:20,897 --> 00:21:22,317
Sea God's Palace?

395
00:21:22,797 --> 00:21:24,557
Okay, but why?

396
00:21:25,957 --> 00:21:27,157
Just a hunch.

397
00:21:27,157 --> 00:21:57,137
Let's make our way to the Sea God's Palace.

398
00:23:06,151 --> 00:23:10,691
One piece Zorro bears his fangs savage animal stands in the way

